# PRD: Pool Renovation Company Website
## Design System: Aspelin Reitan (Candlelit Architectural Archive)
## Stack: React 19 + TypeScript (TSX) + Tailwind CSS

---

## 1. Overview

Build a marketing website for a pool renovation company using the **Aspelin Reitan** design system. The site should read like a curated portfolio of transformed outdoor spaces — full-bleed photography of renovated pools, cream editorial canvases, and whispered typography. The aesthetic is warm, architectural, and gallery-like — not a contractor lead-gen site with loud CTAs.

**Core principle:** The pools and their surrounding architecture carry the brand. The UI is a quiet frame: hairline borders, outlined buttons, no shadows, no fills, no decoration.

---

## 2. Goals & Non-Goals

### Goals
- Present renovation work as an editorial portfolio of built places
- Convey craft, warmth, and permanence through the Aspelin Reitan palette (cream, walnut, amber)
- Drive inquiries through minimal outlined CTAs and a contact form
- Work responsively from 320px to 1440px+
- Ship as a typed, component-driven React application

### Non-Goals
- No e-commerce, pricing calculators, or booking systems
- No blog/CMS beyond a static "Historier" section
- No filled CTA buttons, gradients, shadows, icons, or illustrations
- No display type above 40px, no weights above 500

---

## 3. Target Audience

Homeowners and property managers with existing pools (residential, hotel, estate) considering a full renovation — tile replacement, resurfacing, decking, lighting, and landscape integration. They respond to taste and craftsmanship, not urgency banners.

---

## 4. Technical Stack (Mandatory)

| Layer | Requirement |
|---|---|
| **Framework** | React **19** (use `react@^19`, `react-dom@^19`) |
| **Language** | TypeScript, all components as **`.tsx`** files, `strict: true` |
| **Styling** | **Tailwind CSS v4** using the `@theme` token block from the style reference verbatim |
| **Routing** | React Router v7 (or framework-mode equivalent) — Home, Portfolio, Process, About, Contact |
| **Build tool** | Vite (recommended) or Next.js 15 App Router — either is acceptable, but all page/component code must be `.tsx` |
| **Fonts** | ModernEra if licensed; otherwise self-host Inter or GT America (weights 400/500 only) |
| **Testing** | Vitest + React Testing Library for component tests; Playwright for one visual smoke test per page |

### React 19 specifics
- Use **function components + hooks only** — no class components
- Prefer React 19 features where natural: `use()` for async data (project lists), `useActionState` for the contact form, `useOptimistic` if any stateful UI is added, ref as a prop (no `forwardRef`)
- No legacy `forwardRef`, no `defaultProps`, no `PropTypes`
- Typed props via `interface` / `type` for every component; no `any`

### Tailwind specifics
- Paste the `@theme` block from the style reference directly into `app.css` (or `index.css`), including all color, spacing, text-scale, and radius tokens
- Use token classes only (`bg-warm-parchment`, `text-obsidian`, `text-display`, `gap-100`, `rounded-lg`) — **no arbitrary values** like `bg-[#ffebd0]` or `text-[40px]`
- Enforce the 40px type ceiling and 500 weight ceiling via theme config; do not add larger text tokens
- No Tailwind plugins that introduce shadows, gradients, or new colors

---

## 5. Design System Constraints (Non-Negotiable)

These come directly from the style reference and must be enforced in every component:

### Colors
| Token | Value | Tailwind class | Use |
|---|---|---|---|
| Warm Parchment | `#ffebd0` | `warm-parchment` | Primary canvas |
| Candlelight | `#fff8e9` | `candlelight` | Elevated cream surfaces |
| Obsidian | `#000000` | `obsidian` | Text on cream; 1px borders |
| Walnut Shell | `#2f2116` | `walnut-shell` | Dark sections, footer, photo base |
| Aged Bronze | `#4f3622` | `aged-bronze` | Secondary dark surface/border |
| Amber Glow | `#fee197` | `amber-glow` | Active nav state, single accent |
| Muted Gold | `#987f61` | `muted-gold` | Link borders / underlines on dark |

### Typography
- **Single family:** ModernEra (substitute: Söhne, Inter, or GT America)
- **Weights:** 400 and 500 only
- **Scale:** 16 / 18 / 20 / 24 / 28 / 40px — **never exceed 40px**
- **Line heights:** 1.17–1.40 per the scale table
- Body text: 18px / 1.25 / weight 400

### Shape & Elevation
- Cards & images: **0px radius**, sharp corners, no shadows
- Buttons & links: **8px radius**
- No box-shadows anywhere; depth comes from color contrast and full-bleed photography

### Spacing
- Base unit 4px; spacing scale 8/12/16/20/24/36/40/60/64/100/120
- Page max-width: **1200px**
- Section gap: **100px**
- Card padding: **40px**

### Do / Don't Checklist (enforce in code review)
- ✅ Outlined buttons only (1px Obsidian on cream, 1px Warm Parchment on dark)
- ✅ Full-bleed photography as section anchors, no tint overlays
- ✅ Warm Parchment canvas alternating with Walnut Shell editorial breaks
- ❌ No filled CTAs, shadows, gradients, icons, or illustrations
- ❌ No white text on Warm Parchment
- ❌ No type above 40px or weight above 500
- ❌ No arbitrary Tailwind values; tokens only

---

## 6. Site Map

1. **Home** — full-bleed hero, services intro, featured projects, dark editorial break, contact CTA
2. **Portefølje** (Portfolio) — grid of renovated pools with captions
3. **Prosess** (Process) — how a renovation unfolds (cream canvas, two-column layouts)
4. **Om Oss** (About) — company story, dark editorial section
5. **Kontakt** (Contact) — inquiry form, footer

*Bilingual note: Use Norwegian labels for nav ("Portefølje", "Meny", "Historier") to match the reference's tone, with English body copy if the client prefers, or keep fully localized.*

---

## 7. Page-by-Page Requirements

### 7.1 Global Header
- Transparent, floating over hero imagery
- Wordmark `[COMPANY NAME]` top-left: ModernEra 500, 16–18px, Warm Parchment, wide letter-spacing
- Nav top-right: outlined "Portefølje" button (1px Warm Parchment border, 8px radius, 16–18px h-padding, 6–8px v-padding) + "Meny" text label
- Active nav item: 1px Amber Glow bottom border
- No background fill; over cream sections, swap text/border colors to Obsidian

### 7.2 Home — Hero (Full-Bleed Editorial Hero)
- 100vh photograph of a renovated pool (golden-hour or amber-lit, warm temperature)
- Headline bottom-left: 40px ModernEra 400, Warm Parchment, 40px inset from left/bottom
- Supporting line: 16–18px ModernEra 400, Warm Parchment
- No overlay tint, no scroll indicator icons

### 7.3 Home — Services Section (Cream Canvas)
- Background: Warm Parchment, 1200px max-width, 40px inner padding
- Section heading: ModernEra 500, 24–28px, Obsidian, left-aligned, 40–100px space below
- 3–4 service items (e.g., Re-tiling, Resurfacing, Decking, Lighting) presented as text blocks with ghost links (1px Obsidian bottom border, 8–12px padding-bottom)

### 7.4 Home — Featured Projects (Portfolio Image Cards)
- Single-column or two-column image grid on Warm Parchment
- Images: full-column width, **no border, no radius, no shadow**
- Caption below each: project name at 16px ModernEra 400, Obsidian, 40px padding around text block
- 100px vertical gap between sections

### 7.5 Home — Dark Editorial Break
- Full-bleed warm-toned photograph with Walnut Shell base
- Title top-left: ModernEra 400, 28–40px, Warm Parchment, 40px inset
- Category label "Historier" top-right: 16px Warm Parchment
- No gradient overlay

### 7.6 Portfolio Page
- Intro heading on Warm Parchment (24–28px, ModernEra 500)
- Repeated Portfolio Image Cards; alternate single-column and two-column compositions
- Each caption: project name + short location/scope line at 16px

### 7.7 Project Detail — Two-Column Layout
- Warm Parchment background, 40px padding around group
- Left column ~40% width: square image (sharp corners)
- Right column ~60%: wide exterior image
- Caption below right image: 16px ModernEra 400, Obsidian, left-aligned

### 7.8 Process Page
- Alternating cream content blocks and dark photographic breaks
- Numbered steps as plain text headings (24px ModernEra 500), body at 18px/1.25
- Optional two-column image layout as in 7.7

### 7.9 Contact Page
- Cream canvas, centered 1200px container
- Heading: 28px ModernEra 500, Obsidian
- Form fields: transparent background, 1px Obsidian border, 8px radius, 16px padding, 16px ModernEra 400 text; placeholders at reduced opacity
- Fields: Name, Email, Phone, Pool type (select), Message (textarea)
- Submit: **Outlined Action Button (Cream Section)** — transparent fill, 1px Obsidian border, 8px radius, 18px h-padding, 16px v-padding, ModernEra 500 16px; hover fills Obsidian with Warm Parchment text
- No success modal with icons — a plain text confirmation line below the form
- **Implementation:** wire the form with React 19 `useActionState`; validate client-side; render pending/error/success states as plain text only

### 7.10 Footer
- Walnut Shell background, Warm Parchment text at 16px ModernEra 400
- Single or two-column layout, 40px padding
- Contact details, nav links (ghost links with Muted Gold bottom borders), and any CTA as an outlined button (1px Warm Parchment border)

---

## 8. Component Inventory (`.tsx`)

All components live in `src/components/` and are typed:

| Component | File | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `Header` | `Header.tsx` | Accepts `theme: "dark" \| "light"` for overlay vs. cream sections |
| `Hero` | `Hero.tsx` | Props: `image`, `headline`, `subline` |
| `SectionHeading` | `SectionHeading.tsx` | Props: `children`, optional `as` |
| `OutlinedButton` | `OutlinedButton.tsx` | Props: `variant: "onDark" \| "onCream"`, `href?`, `children`, `type?` — renders `<a>` or `<button>` |
| `GhostLink` | `GhostLink.tsx` | Props: `href`, `theme`, `children` |
| `PortfolioCard` | `PortfolioCard.tsx` | Props: `image`, `alt`, `title`, `meta?` |
| `TwoColumnProject` | `TwoColumnProject.tsx` | Props: `leftImage`, `rightImage`, `caption` |
| `DarkOverlaySection` | `DarkOverlaySection.tsx` | Props: `image`, `title`, `label?` |
| `Input`, `Textarea`, `Select` | `Field.tsx` | Shared field styling component |
| `Footer` | `Footer.tsx` | — |

No component may introduce styles outside the token set. Each component gets a small Vitest + RTL test verifying correct classes and semantics.

---

## 9. Interaction & States

| Element | Default | Hover | Active/Focus |
|---|---|---|---|
| Outlined button (dark bg) | 1px Warm Parchment border, transparent | Border brightens to Candlelight; no fill | Amber Glow border |
| Outlined button (cream bg) | 1px Obsidian border, transparent | Fill Obsidian, text Warm Parchment | — |
| Ghost link | 1px bottom border in context color | No color change; border stays — the line is the affordance | Amber Glow bottom border for nav |
| Input | 1px border, transparent | — | 1px Amber Glow border |
| Nav item | Plain text | — | 1px Amber Glow bottom border |

Transitions: short (150–200ms), opacity/border-color only. No scale, no shadow animation. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

---

## 10. Content Requirements

- **Photography:** Minimum 8–12 high-quality images — renovated pools at golden hour, amber-lit evening shots, pool decks integrated with architecture, before/after pairs in two-column layouts. Warm color temperature mandatory. Documentary, not stock-aspirational.
- **Copy tone:** Restrained, editorial, first-person plural ("Vi former steder..." / "We shape places..."). No exclamation marks, no urgency language.
- **Wordmark:** Company name in all caps, wide letter-spacing.
- **Captions:** Short — project name + location or one-line scope.

---

## 11. Responsive Behavior

- **≥1024px:** Full layouts as specified; two-column grids active; header floats over hero.
- **768–1023px:** Two-column layouts collapse to single column; hero headline stays 40px if it fits, else step to 28px; maintain 60–100px section gaps.
- **<768px:** Single column throughout; 40px insets reduce to 24–36px; hero headline 28px; type scale unchanged otherwise (never below 16px body); header becomes wordmark + "Meny" label only (outlined button may move into a simple menu panel — still outlined, still flat).
- Images always bleed to viewport edge on mobile, sharp corners retained.

---

## 12. Accessibility

- Contrast: Obsidian on Warm Parchment and Warm Parchment on Walnut Shell both pass AA for body sizes. Amber Glow is accent-only — never body text on cream.
- Focus states: 1px Amber Glow border/outline (visible on both canvases), never remove outline without replacement. Use `focus-visible` only.
- All images require descriptive alt text naming the space and renovation scope.
- Form labels always visible (no placeholder-only labels); fields typed and linked via `htmlFor`/`id`.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` — disable all transitions.

---

## 13. Technical Requirements

- **Framework:** React 19 + TypeScript (all `.tsx`), Vite or Next.js 15 App Router
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS v4 with the `@theme` token block from the style reference pasted verbatim into the global stylesheet; token classes only, no arbitrary values
- **Fonts:** Load ModernEra if licensed; otherwise self-host Inter or GT America with weights 400/500 only
- **CSS variables:** The Tailwind `@theme` block must expose the exact tokens from the reference (`--color-warm-parchment`, `--text-display`, `--spacing-100`, `--radius-lg`, etc.)
- **Images:** Serve responsive `srcset`, modern formats (AVIF/WebP), lazy-load below the fold. Hero images preloaded. Use `next/image` if on Next.js, or `<img srcset>` with Vite otherwise.
- **Forms:** React 19 `useActionState` for the contact form; no third-party form library unless justified
- **Testing:** Vitest + RTL component tests; Playwright screenshot smoke test per page (visual regression against the gallery rhythm)
- **Performance:** Lighthouse ≥90 on mobile; no render-blocking third-party scripts
- **SEO:** Semantic landmarks, one H1 per page, meta descriptions, Open Graph image per project

---

## 14. Acceptance Criteria

The build is complete when:

1. Project is React **19** + **TypeScript**, every UI file is `.tsx`, `strict: true`, zero `any`.
2. Tailwind v4 is configured with the reference `@theme` block verbatim; a repo-wide search finds **no arbitrary color/size values** (`bg-[`, `text-[`, `w-[`, `h-[` only allowed for layout where no token exists — and reviewed case by case).
3. Every button on the site is outlined — zero filled CTAs exist in default state (hover fill on cream-section buttons is the only exception, per spec).
4. No element uses box-shadow, gradient, or border-radius other than 0px (images/cards) and 8px (buttons/links/inputs).
5. No text renders above 40px or above weight 500 anywhere.
6. Colors are limited to the seven tokens; Amber Glow appears only on active/focus states and nav accents.
7. Sections alternate Warm Parchment and Walnut Shell full-bleed photography with 100px gaps at desktop.
8. Hero is 100vh, full-bleed, no tint, with 40px bottom-left overlay text.
9. Portfolio images are sharp-cornered and bleed to grid edges with no card containers.
10. Contact form uses React 19 `useActionState`, transparent outlined inputs, and an outlined submit button with the specified hover fill.
11. Passes WCAG AA contrast and keyboard navigation on all interactive elements.
12. Responsive layouts verified at 320 / 768 / 1024 / 1440px.
13. Vitest component tests pass; Playwright smoke screenshots render without layout regressions.

---

## 15. Reference Prompt for the Model

> Build a multi-page pool renovation company website in **React 19 + TypeScript (all `.tsx`) + Tailwind CSS v4** that reads as a candlelit architectural archive. Use the `@theme` token block from the style reference verbatim — Warm Parchment (#ffebd0) as the dominant canvas and Walnut Shell (#2f2116) for dark editorial breaks. Every section is either a full-bleed warm-toned photograph of a renovated pool with a single line of Warm Parchment type bottom-left at 40px ModernEra 400, or a cream canvas with a 1200px contained content block and 40px padding. All buttons are outlined only — 1px borders, 8px radius, no fill except the cream-section hover state that fills Obsidian. No shadows, no gradients, no icons, no radius on images, no type above 40px. Maintain 100px section gaps, 18px/1.25 body text, and hairline borders as the only affordance for links. Use React 19 function components and hooks only; wire the contact form with `useActionState`; type every prop. Use Tailwind token classes exclusively — no arbitrary values. The photography does all the emotional work; the UI whispers.